 "poem": "The current world with many\nHallows and hinds, upon\nThe level of the galley: the\nGauging o' the current.\nBut nivver heard I there his story,\nI, O suer! for all my knowledge. He\nWent to a gallant ship on river\nRhein, he went into it - they only\nSaw him come as hoarse upon\nA-shipwrecked away,\nInto the sea's vast embrace; away.\nAnd through night in danger,",
